	doi = {10.1109/CSAC70128.2026.11607556},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105046618426?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Visual-inertial odometry (VIO) degrades under sensor degradation because conventional systems use handcrafted, brittle degradation heuristics. We propose AdaptVIO, a lightweight adaptive VIO framework incorporating a dualbranch deep learning quality assessment network: MobileNetV3Small scores visual quality (∼ 4 ~ms /frame on CPU) and a threelayer 1D-CNN scores IMU quality (∼ 1 ~ms / window). Quality scores directly scale Extended Kalman Filter measurement noise covariances, continuously modulating each sensor's fusion weight. Both branches train via self-supervised pseudo-labels derived from VIO reprojection error and preintegration residuals-no manual annotation. On all 11 EuRoC MAV sequences, AdaptVIO reduces average ATE by 16.9 % over VINS-Fusion and by 24.6 % on hard visual-degradation sequences, running fully on CPU.  © 2026 IEEE.},
