	doi = {10.1016/j.optlastec.2026.116161},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047338859?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Aiming at the sparse object features in open ground-dominated scenes, relevant studies adopt LiDAR intensity to assist point cloud registration. These methods still suffer from geometric dependence, complicated intensity decoupling, and interference from dynamic noise points. This paper therefore proposes a more robust point cloud inter-frame registration method for such open flat scenes. First, this method initializes the intensity database using ground points of the first frame. Subsequent ground points are retrieved from the database according to ranging values and incident angles, and the intensity ratio is calculated as decoupled relative intensity. Then, special ground points other than dominant ground points are selected based on relative intensity differences, and the database is updated dynamically. Real-time monitoring of the count variation trend of special points is carried out to avoid abnormal extraction of special points caused by type changes of dominant points. Next, the method processes each non-ground point cloud cluster. It constructs a relative distribution descriptor according to the relative spatial relationships between each cluster and neighboring point cloud clusters. Static point cloud clusters are screened through descriptor matching between adjacent frames. Finally, quadrant angle constraints are imposed on special ground points. Inter-frame registration is conducted by combining static non-ground points to obtain valid point cloud registration results. Experimental results show that our method can robustly extract two types of registration feature points in measured scenes. Its root mean square positioning error is 0.14m. This error is reduced by 99.44%, 96.17%, 99.03%, and 98.21% compared with four comparison methods. The single-frame processing time is 0.0364s, featuring excellent real-time processing performance. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd},
	type = {Article},
	publication_stage = {Final},
