	abstract = {For the trajectory tracking problem of unmanned surface vehicles (USVs) under limited computational resources, this paper proposes a hybrid adaptive tiny model predictive control (HAT-MPC) approach. The proposed approach is designed for embedded platforms with limited computational capability while retaining online identification ability. Under certain conditions, effective data are collected online and used for model identification, thereby compensating for prediction errors caused by time-varying model parameters with low computational cost.First, by identifying the unknown system model, the predictive model of the Tiny MPC is updated online, thereby improving the prediction accuracy of the MPC in uncertain environments without significantly increasing the optimization dimensionality. Second, an adaptive penalty factor is introduced into the tiny MPC framework to reduce trajectory tracking errors. Furthermore, to improve tracking efficiency, a virtual vehicle guidance strategy is incorporated to assist the MPC solver. Finally, simulation and field experiments on USV trajectory tracking are conducted to verify the effectiveness of the proposed HAT-MPC method. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.},
