	abstract = {To improve the handling and stability of distributed drive electric vehicles, the study proposes a method integrating high accuracy vehicle state estimation and tire longitudinal and lateral forces prediction. First, based on the seventh-order spherical radius criterion, the proposed square root seventh-order cubature Kalman filter (SR7thCKF) algorithm significantly enhances numerical stability and estimation precision, achieving robust fusion of sensor data and high-accuracy vehicle state parameters (VSPs) estimation. Subsequently, based on the time series characteristics of the estimated VSP and sensor information, the temporal convolutional network (TCN) hierarchically expands the receptive field through dilated causal convolutions, capturing multi-scale temporal patterns, while the gated recurrent unit (GRU) further model global temporal dynamics and long-range dependencies via its adaptive memory gating mechanism. The hyperparameters of the TCN-GRU framework are automatically tuned by Bayesian optimization (BO) algorithm to balance prediction accuracy and computational efficiency, thereby constructing the BO-TCN-GRU model is developed for tire longitudinal and lateral forces prediction. Finally, the results show the high-precision vehicle state estimation of SR7thCKF and the advantage of the hierarchical feature extraction capabilities of BO-TCN-GRU for temporal characteristics. © 2026 IOP Publishing Ltd. All rights, including for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies, are reserved.},
