	abstract = {Aiming at the problem that the error accumulation of MEMS (Micro-Electro-Mechanical Systems) inertial sensors (gyroscopes, accelerometers, magnetometers) in dynamic and complex environments leads to a sharp drop in attitude accuracy, this paper proposed an innovative multi-sensor fusion attitude solution algorithm. Firstly, a quaternion model was established and an adaptive hybrid filtering framework was introduced to quantify the reliability weight of each sensor in the current state in real time. Then, the advantages of complementary filtering and Kalman filtering were intelligently integrated based on weights. Kalman optimal estimation is emphasized when interference is small, and complementary filtering is enhanced to suppress sudden errors during intense motion or strong interference. Finally, a segmented online compensation strategy based on motion recognition is designed. Experiments show that the algorithm reduces the attitude error by 35.41% in dynamic environments, reduces the maximum heading error by 14.37% in magnetic field distortion areas, and reduces the maximum gyro drift error from 5.5° to 2.2° in continuous motion, verifying the effectiveness and practical value of the proposed method in terms of dynamic accuracy, anti-interference and long-term stability. © 2025 IEEE.},
