	abstract = {LiDAR-based simultaneous localization and mapping (SLAM) methods that rely solely on geometric features often fail in degraded environments with sparse or ambiguous structures. We present RTS-SLAM, a visually semantic-enhanced, tightly coupled SLAM framework that integrates semantic point cloud information with principal component analysis (PCA) and Kalman filtering to provide robust priors for dynamic object detection. A visual consistency (VC) subsystem removes dynamic points, while a loop closure module and improved generalized iterative closest point (IGICP)-based LiDAR–inertial mapping and optimization (LIMO) enhance global consistency. By sharing semantic information across modules, RTS-SLAM achieves stable, dense mapping in weakly structured scenes. Experiments on the KITTI dataset and real-world vehicle tests demonstrate competitive performance against state-of-the-art methods. © 2001-2012 IEEE.},
