	abstract = {Aiming at the problem of the degradation of filtering performance caused by the abnormal covariance matrix of system noise in the state estimation process of the untrace Kalman filter, this paper proposes a multi-sensor fusion indoor positioning method based on the improved artificial bee colony optimization algorithm. This paper first constructs a data fusion model that integrates ultra-wideband (UWB), odometer and inertial measurement unit (IMU). Secondly, the improved artificial bee colony algorithm is introduced to conduct dynamic adaptive optimization of the system noise covariance matrix, and the noise characteristics are corrected in real time through the nonlinear optimization process. Then, for the problem of dynamic noise interference, the improved algorithm significantly reduces the interference of dynamic noise changes on state estimation through the population diversity enhancement strategy and the adaptive search mechanism. Finally, the simulation experiments show that, compared with the traditional UKF, the proposed algorithm reduces the average positioning error by approximately 32% in the indoor positioning task of mobile robots, effectively improves the estimation accuracy and robustness of the filter, and ensures the stable convergence of the positioning system in a non-stationary noise environment.  © COPYRIGHT SPIE. Downloading of the abstract is permitted for personal use only.},
