	title = {Context-Aware Sensor Fusion and Mode-Switching Control for an Autonomous Underwater Vehicle},
	year = {2025},
	journal = {2025 17th Seminar on Power Electronics and Control, SEPOC 2025},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/SEPOC67005.2025.11297629},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105032389982?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {This work presents a simulation framework for an Autonomous Underwater Vehicle (AUV) that adapts its control behavior and sensor configuration in response to changing underwater conditions. Implemented in MATLAB Simulink and Simscape, the system integrates a cascaded PID controller with context-aware gain scheduling and sensor morphing logic. Environmental cues such as depth, visibility, and sensor health trigger real-time switching between cruise and maneuver control modes and adaptive sensor fusion using an Inertial Measurement Unit (IMU), a Doppler Velocity Log (DVL), Sonar, and Camera inputs. A Kalman Filter ensures robust state estimation across all configurations. The system is validated in a range of simulated mission scenarios, demonstrating improved energy efficiency, sensor reliability, and trajectory tracking. Results support the use of adaptive control for resilient and efficient underwater navigation.  © 2025 IEEE.},
