	abstract = {Aiming at the complex nonlinear problems in the attitude control of asteroid orbiting probes, this paper proposes an attitude control method based on fully actuated system theory and adaptive iterative learning. The method leverages the characteristics of fully actuated systems to transform the nonlinear system into a linear system with constant coefficients, and incorporates a feedforward-feedback control structure to enhance tracking accuracy and robustness. By constructing a Lyapunov function, the uniform ultimate boundedness of the closed-loop system under bounded disturbances is proven, and the convergence of the control parameter iteration sequence is analyzed using the gradient descent algorithm. Simulation results verify the correctness of the theoretical derivations, demonstrating that the proposed method effectively improves the attitude control performance of probes in complex disturbed environments. Copyright © 2025 The Authors.},
