	abstract = {A robust localization method is presented for autonomous robots in seasonally changing orchards using NDT-matching with edge-based LiDAR segmented data and IMU fusion. By relying on season-invariant structural features, it enhances the accuracy and robustness of localization. The maps of orchard environments across seasons are constructed and the localization performances are calculated under seasonal variations. Using raw points, the average RMSE of four seasons was 9.082 m, reduced to 0.184 m with IMU fusion. For edge points, the average RMSE decreased from 2.699 m to 0.085 m after IMU fusion. In comparison of algorithms, ICP and HDL localization yielded average RMSEs in four seasons of 15.089 m and 2.397 m, respectively. These results demonstrate that the proposed method with edge points and IMU fusion using NDT-matching achieves superior localization accuracy and robustness in seasonally changing orchards. © 2025 IEEE.},
