	abstract = {Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) performing infrastructure monitoring near high voltage transmission lines face reliability challenges from electromagnetic interference and weather disruptions which can lead to crashes. This paper provides a comprehensive reliability analysis and review of machine learning techniques to enable safer and more robust UAV operation. Common UAV failure modes are analyzed, including the effects of electric fields and vibration. Current machine learning techniques that show promise in this domain are evaluated, including neural networks, random forests, and natural language processing. Specific case studies applying these techniques are reviewed and key gaps in research literature and data sharing are identified. Ensembles, onboard sensing improvements, and self-learning UAV approaches have strong future potential to predict failures and analyze reliability in real-time. With sufficient data and advanced algorithms, machine learning will enable enhanced reliability management for UAVs operating near transmission lines and other critical energy infrastructure.  © 2025 IEEE.},
