	abstract = {Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning (AI/ML) have the ability to transform the domain of planetary exploration through the incorporation of real-time autonomous decision-making capabilities in spacecraft. AI methods for spacecraft autonomy consist of supervised ML, which may be centralized or distributed. Centralized, supervised ML is most appropriate for remote-sensing applications. Applications also include in fault-detection and analysis. Unsupervised AI, including generative AI, may also have a role. This paper describes an architecture of an autonomous system designed for planetary navigation. We describe a demonstration rover platform which would be constructed using an enhanced architecture featuring a high-speed AI processing processor. The ultimate aim of our research is to identify the optimal combination of sensors, algorithms and computing platforms that would facilitate autonomous traverse while minimizing power usage and achieving superior operational performance under minimal lighting conditions. The project presents a comprehensive review of the current state-of-the-art for planetary rovers and includes initial recommendations for implementation. Copyright © 2023 by the International Astronautical Federation (IAF). All rights reserved.},
