	abstract = {Underwater, underground, or indoor 3D positioning provides basic support for mobile wireless sensor network(WSN) applications. For 3D positioning, Our laboratory proposed a distributed 3D positioning protocol before——FlagLoc (Flag-based positioning for mobile wireless sensor Network with measurement errors) [1], This algorithm uses a flag consisting of three anchor nodes on an angular plane to begin locating and guiding the network movement of a mobile WSN. In addition, FlagLoc uses a reverse verification mechanism to compensate for range measurement errors. This paper improved the algorithm on the previous results, Fully Connected Neural Network (FCNN) is proposed to solve the initial positioning problem, and a new mechanism is proposed to compensate for the distance measurement error, which is called the second calibration of line segments. The method is as follows: after the initial positioning, each node randomly selects the node next to it for ranging, and then compares and verifies the ranging results with the initial positioning results. The experimental results show that the neural network + line segment second calibration is better than the FlagLoc method on accuracy. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.},
