	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1117/12.3015939},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85197563107?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {This study presents a comprehensive bibliometric analysis of the fusion between quantum tomography and the Extended Kalman Filter (EKF), emphasizing its superiority in refining quantum tomographic reconstructions compared to conventional methodologies. By intersecting quantum mechanical principles with sophisticated filtering technologies, our analysis uncovers emergent research trajectories within the domain of quantum information science. It underscores the significant potential that this integration holds for the evolution of quantum technology applications. Furthermore, this paper delineates the expansive impact of improved quantum state information across a spectrum of scientific fields, thereby enriching the discourse on quantum state estimation and its applications. Through this investigation, we contribute to a deeper understanding of the pivotal role that advanced filtering techniques, specifically the EKF, play in advancing quantum tomography, paving the way for future innovations in quantum computing and beyond. © 2024 SPIE.},
