	abstract = {Localization of Unmanned Ground Vehicle (UGV) in multi-terrain environments, specifically soft terrain, is challenging. High slip scenarios make localization a difficult task. The internal sensors of the UGV are highly dependent on the terrain structure and are prone to errors. Thus, an appropriate measure should be in place to address the mentioned challenges to achieve precise navigation of the UGV. To address this issue, we propose using the GNSS-RTK/IMU/odometer/optical flow-based EKF system to improve state estimation of the UGV and compare it with some legacy approaches. The ground-facing camera will be integrated with image processing techniques such as optical flow to get linear and angular velocities. Additionally, a convolutional neural network (CNN) is used to classify the terrain conditions and update the covariance matrices for the odometer in EKF accordingly. Copyright © 2021 by ASME},
