	abstract = {In this article, an approach for multi-vehicles localization and guiding is described and demonstrated with experiments in real conditions. The general methodology of the presented work is based on a top down approach implemented in each vehicle of the fleet and having a map of the environment to estimate the absolute localization of each vehicle. The principle is to select, at each time, the best set (sensor, detector, landmark) to reach the fixed objective (accuracy and reliability) and thereafter to update the position of the vehicle by using an Extended Kalman Filter and the confidence by using a Bayesian Network. Each vehicle can share its position and its trajectory with the other vehicles in an absolute reference. Thus, a vehicle can track automatically a trajectory shared by another vehicle. Three real experiments demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed approach. © 2017 IEEE.},
